  "overview": {
    "title": "A quarter of memory",
    "p1": "El Jadida’s Mellah is the historic Jewish quarter woven into the wider old town. Lanes are quieter than the main souk arteries; the interest is atmosphere and urban history more than monuments.",
    "p2": "Walk respectfully, keep photography discreet around homes, and use the Mellah as part of a broader medina loop rather than a long standalone stop.",
    "p3": "Pair it with the Portuguese walls and the fishing port for a full reading of the town’s communities and trades."
  },
